Interpretation: look for a lambda where low/mid/high chi2 contributions
are all reasonably close to 1 simultaneously (a 'balanced' row), and
compare its log_evid to the evidence maximum's. If no row achieves that
-- if high-q chi2 only approaches 1 once low/mid q are badly underfit
(chi2 >> 1), or vice versa -- that confirms the imbalance is inherent to
a single global lambda on this kernel/noise structure, not a suboptimal
choice of lambda within Hansen's evidence framework.
